,"role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"FOUNDATIONS §4 Results","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:owner"},{"literal":"a child value keeps its parent's core value","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:choice"},{"literal":"letting a split by cause change the core value, or keeping it","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:among"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:parent-value-rule"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:refinement-maps-once"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:stale-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:stale-satisfied-never-counts"}],"clauses":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"Availability, assessment and acceptance are separate results, each with its own predicate: that a step produced a candidate; that the candidate meets its declared criteria; and that the [decision owner](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation) accepts it at its boundary.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:availability-assessment-acceptance"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:core-only-one","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results"],"statement":"It is defined here once, over the core.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-defined-once"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:gap","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results"],"statement":"A conjunction takes three inputs and keeps them apart: 1. the closed results returned, each a core value with its predicate and domain outcome; 2. the planned assessments that have no closed result applicable to the composite: evaluations the composite requires that were not performed, or whose result is absent, stale, bound to another subject or basis, or incapable of establishing its claim; 3. the required coverage that no planned assessment addresses: for a required obligation set R and the coverage C that the planned assessments admit, the uncovered coverage R minus C.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-three-inputs"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"This core is the only one.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:core-only-one"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:gap","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results"],"statement":"A known failure and a gap of either kind survive every join.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:failure-survives-joins"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:gap","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-three-inputs","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results"],"statement":"A conjunction with any item in the second or third input is never `satisfied`.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:gap-never-satisfied"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:not-performed","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"No refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6): - a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one; - a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to `satisfied`; - an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide: it has no [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped to `indeterminate` or to any other core value; - an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to completed.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:no-mapping-raises-standing"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:not-performed","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"An evaluation that is required or planned and was not performed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it did not perform (P6).","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:not-performed-no-result"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:states","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"Only `satisfied` establishes the predicate.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-satisfied-establishes"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"literal":"recovered: P0's standing in FOUNDATIONS §3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P0 Bounded construction. A finite actor realises a selected outer contract through steps. Each step's selected context fits the actor's envelope.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P1 Interpretation. Subject, representation and interpretation are distinct; meaning holds within a declared context through a declared contract.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P2 Purpose. A selected outcome defines adequacy; interfaces inherit material obligations from the transformation they serve.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P3 Identity. An object's identity is declared (authority, kind, value) and survives admissible change; a boundary is a claim with a proof obligation.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P4b Conservation of step-produced facts. Judgments, residuals, observations and authority decisions the outer contract needs are recorded by the step that produced them.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4b"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P5 Totality. A step can meet a condition outside its context (P0's open-world premise), and it cannot report success on one (P6).","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P6 Justification and authority. Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permits or disposes within scope.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:policy-choice","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"FOUNDATIONS §4 Results","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:owner"},{"literal":"a child value keeps its parent's core value","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:choice"},{"literal":"letting a split by cause change the core value, or keeping it","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:among"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"The parent-value rule governs every such split: each child value names its parent value and its cause and keeps its parent's core value; a child that needs a different core value needs a different parent value, which only the owner of the parent declares; and no child takes `satisfied` from a parent that is not `satisfied`.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:parent-value-rule"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"statement":"A member, profile or adopting Product that needs finer outcomes defines a refinement. The refinement names the question it answers and the predicate its mapping is for, and maps every refined value to exactly one core value.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:refinement-maps-once"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:stale-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results"],"statement":"A stale `satisfied` never counts toward the composite.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:stale-satisfied-never-counts"}],"closure":{"clauses":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:availability-assessment-acceptance","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-defined-once","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-three-inputs","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:core-only-one","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:failure-survives-joins","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:gap-never-satisfied","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:no-mapping-raises-standing","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:not-performed-no-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-satisfied-establishes","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p0","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p1","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p4b","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p5","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:parent-value-rule","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:refinement-maps-once","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:stale-satisfied-never-counts"],"residuals":[],"symbols":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:conjunction","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:core-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:gap","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:not-performed","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:refinement","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:stale-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:policy-choice","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise"]},"frame_indexes":[{"clause_refs":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:availability-assessment-acceptance","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-defined-once","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:conjunction-three-inputs","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:core-only-one","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:failure-survives-joins","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:gap-never-satisfied","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:no-mapping-raises-standing","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:not-performed-no-result","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-satisfied-establishes","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:parent-value-rule","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:refinement-maps-once","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:stale-satisfied-never-counts"],"frame_ref":"stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results","residual_refs":[],"scope":"Combine results or refine result values: the one core algebra, its standing, non-performance, the refinement and parent-value rules, and the conjunction with its three inputs, gaps, stale results and survival.","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results","stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:frame-index:result-algebra-and-conjunction"}],"frame_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#results"],"kind":"axiom-indexer.frame-projection","map_sha256":"sha256:03e058478db63466c8bc6bb03b5e12512397c31f95498d3a1fe3c3fd0526727e","mode":"materialized","program_sha256":"sha256:0caaaed67c1e84def8af0233c73a53db4a94bfc30cbf04bcb7c104da96b0be0d","program_uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:program","projection_sha256":"sha256:430c15ee103a9ffad22c1303fc9008d57c1875df2687987b166057e0090478f6","residual_routes":[],"residuals":[],"resolved_sources":[{"sha256":"sha256